{# ONE PERSON, rendered the same way everywhere.

   Four rows name a person — a member, a group's owner, a project's owner, a
   team's owner — and this is the component all four go through, so a change to
   how a person looks is one change rather than four.

   THE INITIALS CIRCLE IS THIS COMPONENT'S OWN MARKUP. It was a component of its
   own, `avatar`, and this was the only thing that composed it after every direct
   caller was repointed here — a directory a single caller composes is the
   single-caller component this theme forbids. Its lines moved in below,
   unchanged, and its comment came with them because it is still true: THE COLOUR
   IS PASSED IN, NOT DERIVED. A deterministic per-user colour is a decision about
   a user, not about a span, so whoever knows the user picks the key and this
   template only maps the key onto a token. That is also why the enum here is the
   one the circle always had — this component adds no colour vocabulary.

   THE MAIL LINE IS ABSENT, NOT BLANK, when there is none. An app account
   (`bb_agent` in the sample world) has `mail: null`, and a dash there would
   read as an address somebody forgot to fill in rather than as a kind of account
   that has none. The name alone is the whole truth for such a row.

   `compact` IS ONE LINE AND NO MAIL, and its name is optional on purpose. Every
   caller that used to place the bare circle — the user menu, the workspace
   switcher, a team row in the nav, a comment's author, a ticket row's assignee —
   already renders its own label beside it, with its own truncation and its own
   collapse behaviour, so a name forced out of this template would be a second
   copy of one they already have. Pass a `display_name` and `compact` is the
   circle and the name on one line; leave it out and `compact` is the circle,
   which is exactly what the deleted component was.

   `picture` REPLACES THE CIRCLE, NOT THE FALLBACK (BB-507): a rendered image
   URL swaps the initials mark for an `<img>` of the same size and shape; without
   one, the initials circle is unchanged. `image_fit` chooses how the image
   fills the mark: `cover` (the default, every account picture) crops to the
   circle, `contain` centres the whole image uncropped, for a project or group
   image of any aspect ratio, on a neutral surface instead of the colour key
   so the letterbox around a non-square image reads as a frame.

   `profile` IS THE SUBJECT OF A WHOLE PAGE — the account overview on
   `/user/{user}`: a large mark centred above the name in the display role,
   `subtitle` beneath it, and no mail. `subtitle` is one secondary line (the
   developer title); `full` renders it too, `compact` has no room for it. #}
{% set compact = variant == 'compact' %}
{% set profile = variant == 'profile' %}
{# Avatars have their own fills, so a person never reads as a state. #}
{% set color_map = {
  'running': 'bg-avatar-a',
  'attention': 'bg-avatar-b',
  'unassigned': 'bg-avatar-a',
  'lease': 'bg-avatar-c',
  'offline': 'bg-avatar-d'
} %}
{% set size_classes = profile ? 'w-20 h-20 text-page-title' : (size == 'md' ? 'w-7 h-7 text-badge' : 'w-6 h-6 text-badge') %}
{% set mark_classes = ['inline-grid', 'place-items-center', 'rounded-full', 'shrink-0', 'overflow-hidden', 'text-state-ink', size_classes, color_map[color]|default('bg-avatar-a')] %}
{% set stack_gap = profile ? 'gap-stack' : (size == 'md' ? 'gap-inline' : 'gap-inline-xs') %}
{% set root_classes = profile ? ['flex', 'flex-col', 'items-center', 'text-center', stack_gap, 'min-w-0'] : ['inline-flex', 'items-center', stack_gap, 'min-w-0'] %}
{% set identity %}
<span{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(root_classes) }}>
  {%- if picture %}
    <img data-person-mark class="{{ (image_fit == 'contain' ? mark_classes|filter(c => not (c starts with 'bg-'))|merge(['object-contain', 'object-center', 'bg-surface-2', 'border', 'border-border-2']) : mark_classes|merge(['object-cover']))|join(' ') }}" src="{{ picture }}" alt="" />
  {%- else %}
    <span data-person-mark class="{{ mark_classes|join(' ') }}">{{ initials }}</span>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if compact %}
    {%- if display_name %}<span class="truncate text-body-strong text-text" title="{{ display_name }}" data-collapse-hidden>{{ display_name }}</span>{% endif %}
  {%- elseif profile %}
    <span class="flex flex-col items-center gap-inline-xs min-w-0">
      <span class="text-page-title font-display text-text">{{ display_name|default(initials) }}</span>
      {%- if subtitle %}<span class="text-body text-text-light">{{ subtitle }}</span>{% endif %}
    </span>
  {%- else %}
    <span class="flex flex-col min-w-0 leading-tight">
      <span class="truncate text-body-strong text-text" title="{{ display_name|default(initials) }}">{{ display_name|default(initials) }}</span>
      {%- if subtitle and subtitle_datetime %}{{ include('bb_theme:time', { label: subtitle, datetime: subtitle_datetime, title: subtitle_title|default(''), attributes: create_attribute({ class: ['truncate', 'text-meta', 'text-text-light'] }) }, with_context = false) }}
      {%- elseif subtitle %}<span class="truncate text-meta text-text-light" title="{{ subtitle }}">{{ subtitle }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if mail %}<span class="truncate text-meta text-text-faint" title="{{ mail }}">{{ mail }}</span>{% endif %}
    </span>
  {%- endif %}
</span>
{% endset %}
{%- if url -%}
  <a href="{{ url }}" class="min-w-0 no-underline text-inherit focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus-ring">{{ identity }}</a>
{%- else -%}
  {{ identity }}
{%- endif -%}
